menu "InertialSaber"

    config SABER_PARSER_SELF_TEST
        bool "Run the profile parser self-test at boot"
        default y
        help
            Runs ProfileParser::runSelfTest() before the hardware is initialised.
            A failing self-test aborts the boot with the error status.
            Disable it in release builds to shorten the boot and save flash.

    config SABER_METRICS
        bool "Record real-time metrics and write them to /sdcard/metrics"
        default y
        select HEAP_USE_HOOKS
        help
            Records bus cycle and effect run() timings, loop and IMU rates, event
            counters, heap allocations per CPU core, free heap and task stack
            high-water marks in under 0.5 KB of internal RAM, without heap use or
            locks on the real-time path. A priority-1 task (4 KB stack, about 10 KB of
            PSRAM buffers) appends one CSV block per ignition session to
            /sdcard/metrics/session_NNN.csv, only while the saber is retracted
            and the audio is idle. Enables the heap allocation hooks.
            When disabled, the instrumentation compiles to nothing.
            Disable it in release builds.

endmenu
